course: dictionary
lesson: 2521
title: Declare: saying it clearly
level: primary-5
stars: 3
explain: To declare something is to say it clearly, firmly or officially, so everyone knows. «Kai declared it the most unfair rule in the history of the world.» Kai did not mumble. He said his strong opinion out loud so everyone heard it.
explain: Look at the words after declare to find its meaning. In «Britain and France declared war», the word war is the clue: to declare war is to announce officially that a war is starting. Check by swapping in announced: «Britain and France announced war» is not quite right, but «announced that a war was starting» makes the meaning clear.
explain: Declare also means telling officials about goods you bring into a country. At customs, a traveller who says «nothing to declare» means they have no goods to tell the officials about. The same word works in a different place, so read the whole sentence for the clue.
fact: Declare means to say something clearly, firmly or officially, so everyone knows.
fact: «Declare war» means to announce officially that a war is starting.
fact: «Declare independence» means to announce officially that a country is free and no longer ruled by another country.
fact: At customs, to declare goods means to tell officials what you are bringing into a country.
fact: «The Chinese paddlefish was declared extinct in 2020» means officials announced that this fish had died out.
exercise: «Kai declared it the most unfair rule in the history of the world.» What does declared mean here? | Whispered quietly to a friend | Wrote it down years later | Forgot all about it | *Said firmly and clearly, so everyone knows
exercise: «In September 1939 Germany invaded Poland, and Britain and France declared war.» What does declared war mean? | *Officially announced that a war was starting | Ended a war | Hid from a war | Won a war
exercise: «Smallpox was declared done in 1980.» Find and copy one word that means officially announced. | 1980 | smallpox | done | *declared
test: A traveller at the airport says «nothing to declare». What does this mean? | Their bags are lost | They want to be a customs officer | *They have no goods to tell the officials about | They are feeling sad
test: «Polls in Taiwan have shown most people want to keep things as they are, neither declaring full independence nor joining China.» What does declaring full independence mean? | Asking people for their opinions | Joining a school club | Staying exactly the same | *Officially announcing that they are fully free
exam: A cricket captain declares the innings closed early. What does declares mean here? | *Announces officially that the innings is over early | Asks the umpire for a drink | Starts the game again | Hits the ball very hard
